==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of [[red]] + [[neck]] (referring to the sunburn on the neck; typical of rural farm workers).

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang}} An uneducated, unsophisticated, or poor white person, typically used to describe residents of the [[rural]] Southern US.  A redneck can be a man or a woman <ref>http://www.hit-country-music-lyrics.com/redneck-woman-lyrics.html</ref>
# {{context|slang}} The nickname given to miners who wore red bandanas for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.  <ref>http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html</ref>

